# ULPF raw archive record (static). One JSON line per received event.
# raw_b64 holds the exact received bytes; raw_sha256/raw_len were computed in
# the envelope from the same bytes.
#
# The record is serialised here (encode_json: sorted keys, byte-identical to
# Vector's json codec) into `message`, so that a reduce transform can batch
# many lines into one file write: Vector 0.58's file sink issues one write
# per event and managed ~210 events/s on the reference VM (P6 finding).
#
# `timestamp` is only used by the file sink's path template. It is the
# *archive write time*, not the receipt time: if backpressure delays an event,
# it lands in the current minute file instead of re-opening a file that
# `ulpf seal` may already have sealed. The receipt time is in ingest_time.
raw = string!(._raw)
rec = {
  "v": 1,
  "event_uid": .ulpf.event_uid,
  "ingest_time": .ulpf.ingest.time,
  "collector_id": .ulpf.ingest.collector_id,
  "transport": .ulpf.ingest.transport,
  "peer": .ulpf.ingest.peer,
  "raw_len": .ulpf.raw.len,
  "raw_sha256": .ulpf.raw.sha256,
  "raw_b64": encode_base64(raw)
}
. = {"message": encode_json(rec), "timestamp": now()}
